    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01905v1</id>
    <title>Some refinements of Hermite-Hadamard inequality and an open problem</title>
    <updated>2016-11-07T06:35:42Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01905v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1611.01905v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We presented here a refinement of Hermite-Hadamard inequality as a linear combination of its end-points. The problem of best possible constants is closely connected with well known Simpson's rule in numerical integration. It is solved here for a wide class of convex functions, but not in general. Some supplementary results are also given.</summary>
